  "anchor_definition": "a probe centred at age a occupies source time -a within 3 half widths; the anchor is the youngest age on the common grid whose whole probe support lies inside the reachable source-time window [min(t_obs) - max(delay), max(t_obs) - min(delay)]. Where the minimum delay exceeds the last observer sample the anchor is a positive age and the present is simply not observed",
  "anchored_stable_depth": "T_stable_anchor(eps,q) = sup{ T >= a_anchor : Pr[ sup_{a_anchor <= a <= T} E(a) <= eps ] >= q }; the supremum over the age window is inside the probability, taken per truth, so a truth counts only if the whole window from the anchor out to T is good for that truth",
  "anchored_stable_span": "L_stable_anchor = T_stable_anchor - a_anchor",
  "prohibition": "an arbitrary old detectable island is never labelled continuous history from the anchor; a secondary unanchored longest stable interval may be reported with both endpoints but must not be called depth from the present",
